NOTES.md
# --- .rclaude/ : the project board is TRACKED, everything else is not --------
# The board (`.rclaude/project/`) is the only durable copy there is. The broker
# backup covers the broker's own cacheDir and structurally cannot reach into a
# project tree (CWD IS INFORMATIONAL, lint:boundary Rule 4), so git IS the
# backup. See docs/backup.md.
#
# Order matters, and so does `*`. Git never descends into an excluded
# DIRECTORY, so `.rclaude/` + a nested `!project/` re-include is a no-op that
# fails silently -- that was the live bug until 2026-08-21. Exclude the
# CONTENTS instead, then negate.
#
# Guarded both directions by src/shared/board-gitignore.test.ts. Over-correcting
# here stages `.rclaude/settings/` -- 687 MB, measured.
#
# any .rclaude/ anywhere (worktrees, nested projects) stays fully ignored ...
.rclaude/
# ... except the one at the repo root, whose contents we then filter by hand
!/.rclaude/
/.rclaude/*
!/.rclaude/project/
!/.rclaude/rclaude.json
# machine-local snapshot from the lane-folder -> frontmatter migration; the
# board tooling already treats this prefix as not-a-card (project-doctor-layout)
/.rclaude/project/.upgrade-backup-*/
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
.nightshift/
.launchfile/
.env.local
/store.db
/store.db-shm
/store.db-wal
design/
